        terrazzo_h2_advantages: "Key Advantages",
        terrazzo_adv1: "<strong>Exceptional Longevity</strong> \u2014 50+ year service life. Many terrazzo floors installed in the 1920s still perform today.",
        terrazzo_adv2: "<strong>Design Freedom</strong> \u2014 Unlimited colors, patterns, logos, and inlays. True custom design capability.",
        terrazzo_adv3: "<strong>Low Lifecycle Cost</strong> \u2014 Higher upfront cost offset by decades of service. Restorable, not replaceable.",
        terrazzo_adv4: "<strong>Sustainable</strong> \u2014 Recycled glass and post-consumer aggregates. VOC-free cement systems. LEED credits.",
        terrazzo_adv5: "<strong>Seamless & Hygienic</strong> \u2014 No grout lines. Divider strips are integral. Easy to clean and maintain.",
        terrazzo_adv6: "<strong>Restorable</strong> \u2014 Can be reground and repolished to original condition. Floor that improves with age.",
        terrazzo_h2_maintenance: "Maintenance Protocol",
